 those situations where i wouldn't blame  either anime watchers or margaritas for  not remembering this character in the  2011 anime he is shown in episode 58 for  a handful of seconds and never named and  the mainline manga doesn't get much  better because he's only ever shown in  two panels although to be fair one of  those panels does at least have his name  but the bulk of information we have  concerning pyro comes from the special  hunter hunter volume zero which consists  of two chapters entitled kerapika's  memories which take us through  karapika's memories funny that but in  this we become very familiar with the  young pyro who was also a member of the  kodaklan and there are several layers of  tragedy concerning him the first is that  in an attempt to save karapika from  falling off a cliff pyro in an event  that i can only describe as somehow  actually ended up severely injuring both  his legs and his eyes a very interesting  combination of bodily things there and  dies of course being a very important  aspect of any kurt clan member so let's  not blast past that yet it will become  relevant later but this is what provided  krapika with the motivation to travel to  the outside world he wanted to find some  sort of medicine to cure pyro and look  long story less long that is why krapika  ended up outside of the village when the  phantom troop massacred the rest of the  clan so in a very like very twisted way  pyro's original tragedy paved the way  for a second tragedy as karapika was  saddled with the self-given task of  vengeance for his clan but we do learn  later on that part of this drive is to  recover the parts of pyro that were  taken and i should also note that this  material is incorporated as part of the  film hunter hunter phantom rouge but  look there's all sorts of like weird  non-canon stuff mixed in as well because  the plot heavily features a modern day  pyro doll sort of thing and apparently  it's an alternate retelling of york new  city that togashi had originally planned  but look there's a reason why it was  scrapped so let's just let's move on  back to relevant things now the next  question you may have is hey new old guy  yeah sure that head looks vaguely like  pyro but why would anyone go to the  trouble of keeping the head when the  only valuable thing about the curt clan  are the scarlet eyes well this question  is answered incredibly briefly even  forgettably in the manga during york  knew when krapika is infiltrating the  strat family he is presented with a test  and of course in a moment of great  traumatic irony his test is to acquire a  set of scarlet eyes now in the 2011  anime we see a shot of eyes and jars and  that's it but the manga goes into  slightly more detail because krapika's  instructions to acquire the eyes were as  follows curta eyeballs must be scarlet a  complete set with head preferred  difficulty level a so we do know that  for whatever reason there were cases  where entire curta heads were harvested  although given that currently in the  manga every set of scarlet eyes has been  accounted for we also know that this  head here sitting as the centerpiece of  sradnik's disgusting body part  collection is a one of a kind it is the  only head with a complete set of scarlet  eyes in the entire world so we've  established that this is definitely a  curta head but why is this pyro well to  answer that we need to engage in a bit  of narrative dumbing down firstly we  have met a lot of kurt clan members  mostly in volume zero none of which have  pyro's bowl cut hair style secondly as  we have a direct comparison to sirenix  head this curtain noggin clearly belongs  to a child and thirdly i know that  togashi sometimes forgets or let's be  real completely disregards plot points  that he set up but i find it very  difficult to believe that even he would  deliberately design a completely  separate curta clan childhood that just  so happens to look exactly like someone  dramatically relevant like say pyro is  it possible  i guess is it likely though  i don't think so here's the real kicker  though we also know for a fact that  pyro's body was harvested because in  chapter 344 after discovering where the  last of the eyes are karapika states but  this will soon end this is the last  monster with the last of the eyes among  them pyro so pyro is definitely part of  saradnick's collection and i would  personally find it really odd if he  happened to be two of the lone eyeballs  as opposed to the head in the center  that looks exactly like him i mean to be  fair tagashi has done weirder things in  the past he's unpredictable and he  sometimes does so confusion for the sake  of confusion but until that happens i  think we need to go with the occam's  razor explanation because the simplest  one is usually the correct one either  way what i'm really interested in is why  pyro's head was kept intact as opposed  to the other kurta members and i would  posit that it likely has something to do  with his aforementioned eye injury  whoever was harvesting the eyes may have  picked up on this and decided that it  would be too risky to remove them from  the head or perhaps that injury had the  sickening effect of somehow making  pyro's eyes even more special in some  sort of way so they decided to keep them  in the head as a sort of super special  collector's edition which once again is  a sickening thought but that's the way  you need to think about these kind of  characters in fact whenever the topic of  body part collecting comes up in hunter  hunter i'm always reminded of karapika's  words in chapter 67. there are two  things collectors want one is rare and  valuable items the other is friends to  whom they can brag about their  collection which brings us to the ever  important saradnik even before this pyro  thought was brought up the fourth prince  of the khaking empire was clearly being  set up as a direct photographical you  know they're both nen geniuses both  interested in scarlet eyes and they are  of course both floppy mop-headed blondes  it's as good a match as we will ever see  and with karapika directly representing  an opposing prince in the succession war  this conflict was going to happen  eventually and i guess we should also  take a moment to remind everyone that  ceranic's entire collection is indeed  aboard the black whale one because the  khaking empire are treating this voyage  as a permanent move their intention is  to settle on the dark continent and  develop an even more powerful nation  with all of the benefits that the dark  continent can provide them so very  interestingly both krapika and pyro were  in the same place at the same time for  the first time in many units of time  what's unclear at this stage is if  krapika knows that pyro's whole head  remains intact in fact the entire  harvesting process is rather thankfully  unclear but if i was writing a story i  feel like maximum drama would be  achieved if krapika did not know and  then suddenly he was confronted with the  preserved image of his best friend and i  have no doubt that this would throw him  into a rage the likes of which we have  never seen which is going to end up like  a domino effect into even more drama  because the other story thread being set  up here is krapika's loyalty and duty to  prince wobile and it may even come down  to an ultimate choice between closure  for the kurt clan and securing the  safety of wobel and in that case what  would he prioritize vengeance for those  long past or the future for someone  whose time has barely begun it's a rough  choice for sure but then again that kind  of summarizes kraupker's entire  existence and whatever the case this is  very much set up to be his character  climax in the series to add to all of  the stuff we also mustn't forget that  the phantom troop are also aboard the  blackwell one and while karapika has  theoretically left that revenge quest to  die we do still have hints of this  thread potentially becoming important  specifically from zodiac member  mizeistom who very much struggled with  the decision of whether or not to tell  krapika about their presence and if this  was any other series then i would take  this as a definite piece of  foreshadowing however as per usual this  is hunter hunter and togashi could just  be playing out the realistic thoughts of  mizeistom without any intention of doing  something grander with them to act as  more of a character study of mizeistom  than having him just opine for the sake  of story and the narrative and the stuff  and while i don't necessarily agree with  this next thought i do feel the need to  mention it because whenever this whole  pyro head business is brought up there  is another sub theory that emerges  stating that pyro's head could be  incorporated into sradnik's guardian nen  beast and to be fair the head within a  head does look very like very vaguely  like the pyro with shaped head in the  jar but this is where the gaping logic  chasm just becomes a bit too much of a  leap for me mostly because this nan  beast is designed to explore an entirely  different idea this is radnick's  manifestation of women in his life or at  least his feelings towards women in his  life who seem to exist to be butchered  and their remains transformed into fine  art and i do think that this head could  just as easily belong to this woman who  we saw into his hotel room to continue  to be fair though sradnik did not choose  the form of this nen beast it was  manifested as part of the sidon ceremony  so perhaps if pyro's head is so  important to the fourth prince it is the  centerpiece of his collection after all  then its image may also have been  incorporated into the guardian nen beast  and i have to say that would also be  quite dramatic for karapika to come face  to face with the head of his childhood  friend trapped within this greater like  horrific monster thing once again though  it's just a step too far for me  everything about this nin b so far has  been very much geared towards women even  its abilities which thus far have only  targeted women to add to that in the  rare other images we have of the head  within another head the haircut appears  to be much less similar to that of pyro  and more of a central part than a clean  bowl cut so i think that pyro's head  remains here and here alone and you know  with all of this head talk we haven't  even begun to discuss the radnick's  throne this thing is like pure  necromancy although i do love the heads  on either side of ceratnic because they  look like your classical devil and angel  on each shoulder style of situation  forever trying to talk ceradnik into  doing stupid things i think you should  show everyone your penis my lord you  know usually i disagree with that guy  but i think that's a good idea hmm do it  my lord yeah look i i don't see why not  do it do it do it do it theta i've made  a decision  you know that would actually explain  quite a bit about sirednik but i suppose  the real question we're left with is the  outcome right now krapika has done  everything he can on his quest to avoid  murdering someone except for the one guy  that he murdered but ever since then  he's made a career of threatening  tricking and bargaining with people to  retrieve the eyes of his clan members  but something tells me that none of  those methods are quite going to work  with saratnik and after seeing pyro's  head i'm really not too sure that  karapika will be in any sort of  bargaining mood either however he will  be in the mood for another video like  this one which is also about hunter  hunter because there's always more to  learn exploring experience with this  wonderful series so i look forward to  seeing you there

